# Do not commit/push on your own

- NEVER run `git commit`, `git push`, `git merge`, `git rebase`, or otherwise
  create/rewrite history unless the user explicitly asks (e.g. "提交" / "推送" /
  "commit" / "push").
- After making code changes, stop at leaving the working tree modified. It is
  fine to build, flash, run, and test, but do not stage-and-commit as a
  "finishing" step.
- When the user does ask to commit, only then commit (and push only if they ask
  to push).
- If you think a commit is warranted, you may suggest it — but wait for the user
  to confirm before doing it.
